# oracle: fix colvars in a triclinic LJ box (prism 1.0 0.5 -0.7: the Colvars minimum image with its neighbour-cell search), unwrap no, a configuration given by fix_modify config in triple quotes with a $(v_a) reference (substituted when fix colvars reads it), run 0 (the step is not advanced), a second configuration from fix_modify configfile between runs (the traj label is written again), and a minimization (min_post_force; the step advances once per iteration, before its line search, so the traj repeats a step for each line-search evaluation)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native: thermo 4.4e-15, final atoms 6.1e-13, state file byte-identical, traj 5e-15 (the same 51 lines, repeated steps included).
# oracle-inputs: w762cv_tri.colvars
# oracle-files: tri.colvars.traj tri.colvars.state
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 filerel=1e-10
units           lj
atom_modify     map yes
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box prism 0 4 0 4 0 4 1.0 0.5 -0.7
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
velocity        all create 1.2 4928459 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
variable        a equal 200
fix             1 all nve
fix             2 all colvars none output tri unwrap no
fix_modify      2 config """
  colvarsTrajFrequency 2
  colvar {
    name dv
    distanceVec {
      group1 { atomNumbers 3 }
      group2 { atomNumbers $(v_a) 201 }
    }
  }
  harmonic {
    colvars dv
    centers (0.5, 0.2, -0.3)
    forceConstant 2.0
  }
"""
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal f_2 f_2[1][1] f_2[1][2] f_2[1][3]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             0
run             20
fix_modify      2 configfile w762cv_tri.colvars
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal f_2 f_2[1][1] f_2[1][2] f_2[1][3] f_2[2][1]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             20
minimize        1.0e-12 1.0e-12 30 100
